From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui i18n: Czech, Hungarian, Polish, Turkish, Vietnamese, Croatian, Italian, Bulgarian and Swedish rows for the strings of patches 0136 and 0137

Patches 0136 (File > Print wording) and 0137 (Document Recovery pane) added 19 strings to ru.tsv. Upstream's own catalog tests
(czech/hungarian/polish/turkish/vietnamese/croatian_covers_*) require these catalogs to hold every key of ru, so they failed
('cs lacks ru's [...]'); the Italian test requires it to hold every key of tr, and the untranslated-text audit requires the
complete catalogs (ru hu tr bg it sv hr pl) to hold every string the interface looks up. The 19 rows go to cs, hu, pl, tr, vi,
hr and it; the one account-tip row also to bg and sv. Under an office overlay comment; machine-translation drafts of short
interface strings by the agent, not reviewed by a native speaker. No other catalog is compared with ru by a test.
---

